# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit real values.
# Every new variable must be added here in the same commit that introduces it.

# --- Model provider (pick at least one) -----------------------------------------------------
# The agent is provider-agnostic on purpose: the evaluation harness scores whichever model is
# configured, so "which model" is a measured result rather than an assumption, and the same
# question set can be replayed across providers on identical ground truth.

# Google Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# xAI Grok — https://console.x.ai
# XAI_API_KEY=

# Local Ollama needs no key, only a running server:
#   ollama serve
#   ollama pull qwen3        (any tool-calling model; qwen3 is the default)
# Override the endpoint only if it is not on the default port.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1

# --- Science service ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the Python service listens. The agent runs server-side and calls it directly, so this is
# needed even though the browser reaches the same service through a rewrite.
# Port 8787 rather than 8000: on Windows, 8000 and 9000 sit in Hyper-V reserved ranges and
# refuse to bind with WinError 10013.
# SCIENCE_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# --- Space-Track (evaluation ground truth only) ---------------------------------------------
# MUST NOT be set on the public deployment: the public app serves Celestrak data, which needs no
# authentication. This split keeps the deployment clearly inside Space-Track's redistribution
# terms.
# SPACETRACK_USERNAME=
# SPACETRACK_PASSWORD=
